Internship Preparation Method
1. Identify Your Target Domain

Core Mechanical: HVAC, Thermal Systems, CAD Design, Manufacturing, Maintenance.

Advanced Tech Integration: Robotics, Automation, AI in Mechanical, Simulation (CFD, FEA).

Industry Type: Automotive, HVAC, Aerospace, Energy, Power Plants, Textile (relevant for you).

2. Build a Strong Foundation

✔ Refresh Core Subjects:

Thermodynamics (Power cycles, Heat transfer)

Fluid Mechanics (HVAC relevance)

Strength of Materials

Machine Design

✔ Simulation & CAD Tools:

SolidWorks / CATIA → Part Modeling, Assemblies, Simulation

ANSYS → Structural, Thermal Analysis

MATLAB → Control Systems, Numerical Analysis

AutoCAD → Drafting

✔ Programming Basics (for automation & ML):

Python (Basics + NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib)

MATLAB scripts

Basics of ML applications in design (Predictive Maintenance, Optimization)

3. Create Internship-Ready Resume & Portfolio

Resume:

Focus on projects → Include CAD designs, simulations, or coding projects.

Use ATS-friendly keywords (Mechanical Design, SolidWorks, Thermal Analysis, MATLAB, Python).

Portfolio (GitHub/LinkedIn):

Upload design models, simulation reports, Python scripts.

Share write-ups on LinkedIn about your learning journey.

4. Practice Interview & Technical Questions

Mechanical Core Questions:

Laws of Thermodynamics, HVAC cycle, Stress & Strain analysis.

Bearings, Gears, Joints, and Material selection.

Software-based Questions:

“How do you perform stress analysis in SolidWorks?”

“Difference between FEA and CFD?”

Behavioral Questions:

“Why do you want this internship?”

“Tell me about a project where you solved a problem.”

5. Apply to Internships

✔ Platforms:

LinkedIn Jobs

Rozee.pk

Interns.pk

Company Websites (Textile, HVAC, Power Plants, etc.)

Global: Internshala, Indeed, Glassdoor

✔ Networking:

Contact seniors & alumni.

Join Mechanical Engineering + AI groups on LinkedIn.

6. Prepare Soft Skills

Communication: Explain technical concepts in simple terms.

Presentation: Use PowerPoint for project presentations.

Teamwork: Highlight any group projects.

